From f93a1cc85468de841205e944aec5f38719751dcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ying <thisisytee@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 10:59:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: implement MCP_SERVER object type for Snowflake-managed
 Cortex Agents
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds full SnowDDL support for Snowflake's managed MCP server (Cortex
Agents MCP) — see https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/snowflake-cortex/cortex-agents-mcp.

Schema-object YAML lives under <db>/<schema>/mcp_server/<name>.yaml and
accepts:

  tools:
    - name: ...
      type: CORTEX_SEARCH_SERVICE_QUERY|CORTEX_ANALYST_MESSAGE|CORTEX_AGENT_RUN|SYSTEM_EXECUTE_SQL|GENERIC
      title|description|identifier: ...
      <type-specific fields passed through verbatim>
  spec_extra: { ... }
  comment: ...

Resolver renders YAML into CREATE OR REPLACE MCP SERVER ... FROM
SPECIFICATION $$ ... $$ and embeds a short-hash in COMMENT for drift
detection (mirrors SemanticView; ALTER MCP SERVER for tools is not yet
exposed by Snowflake).

RBAC: default permission model now grants CREATE MCP SERVER + future
OWNERSHIP on MCP SERVERS to schema OWNER, future USAGE on MCP SERVERS
to schema READ.
